Chapter: LensPlan
  cites Lens chapter LensModel
  cites Data chapter Row
  cites Data chapter RelAlgebra
  cites Data chapter Executor
  cites Data chapter Catalog

 The planner turns a LensQuery into a grain-correct relational plan.
 The v1 rule is structural, per the design's fan-out section: every
 measure is aggregated at the grain of its own home table before any
 join. A measure whose home table already carries every requested
 dimension aggregates directly, with no join at all. A measure that
 must reach a dimension on another table first groups its home table
 by the join keys, then equi-joins the already-aggregated rows to the
 dimension tables, then re-aggregates by the dimension columns. Sum
 re-aggregates as sum, count as a sum of counts, min as min, max as
 max. An average is never re-aggregated: the planner decomposes it
 into a sum and a count over the same column, both at the home
 grain, carries the pair through every join and re-aggregation as
 sums, and lens-run divides the pair once after the last combine.
 The division is integer division in v1, the same truncation the
 engine's own average applies. Fan-out never reaches an aggregate
 because nothing is summed after a row can be duplicated.

 A dimension's table is reached by a chain of declared many-to-one
 joins walked from the measure's home table, up to four hops deep. A
 chain of many-to-one hops is grain-safe because every hop maps many
 rows to one, so the aggregated home rows never multiply on the way
 to the dimension. A table no chain reaches earns diagnostic 23, and
 a table two distinct chains reach earns diagnostic 28, because the
 planner refuses to pick a join path silently.

 Query filters are equality tests on physical columns. A filter lands
 on every scan of the table it names, under every aggregation,
 therefore a filter always applies at raw-row grain: a filter on a
 measure's home table restricts the rows that sub-aggregation sums,
 and a filter on a dimension table restricts the dimension rows every
 sub-plan joins against. A filter naming a table or column outside
 the model's vocabulary, or a table the query never touches, is
 rejected with diagnostic 27.

 Result columns are physical names: each dimension contributes its
 column name and each measure contributes its measure name as the
 aggregate alias. An average travels through the plan as two columns,
 the measure name suffixed __sum and __cnt, and lens-run replaces the
 pair with the single measure-name column holding their quotient, so
 a caller sees exactly the columns it asked for. A measure named to
 collide with another measure's __sum or __cnt spelling would break
 the pairing; v1 accepts that assumption rather than police names.
 Rows sort ascending by the dimension columns so results are
 deterministic, and a positive limit truncates after the sort. A
 limit of zero means no limit.

Section: Plan Result

 lens-plan answers with a plan or with diagnostics, never both. When
 plan-ok is False the plan-op field holds an inert placeholder scan
 and only plan-diags speaks. The plan-avgs field names the average
 measures whose sum-and-count column pairs lens-run must divide after
 execution; it is empty whenever the query names no averages. Planner
 diagnostics draw from code 20 upward; codes 1 through 7 belong to
 the model validator. The table:

 code 20 means the query names a lens this model does not declare.
 code 21 means a queried dimension name is not in the model.
 code 22 means a queried measure name is not in the model.
 code 23 means no chain of many-to-one joins reaches a dimension's
 table from a measure's home table within four hops.
 code 24 means the query names no measures.
 code 25 is retired: it refused average measures that would need
 re-aggregation across a join. The planner now decomposes every
 average into a sum and a count at the home grain, re-aggregates the
 pair losslessly, and lens-run divides after the last combine,
 therefore the code is never issued again.
 code 26 is retired: it refused several measures with several
 dimensions when the combine step was a single-column equi-join. The
 combine step now equi-joins on the full requested-dimension column
 set, therefore the shape plans correctly and the code is never
 issued again.
 code 27 means a query filter names a table or column this query
 cannot filter: the table is not declared, the column is not part of
 the model's vocabulary for that table, or the table takes no part in
 the query.
 code 28 means more than one distinct chain of many-to-one joins
 reaches a dimension's table from a measure's home table. The message
 names two of the paths; the modeler must remove a join or query a
 different shape, because the planner will not pick between paths
 silently.

  LensPlanResult = record {
    plan-ok : Boolean,
    plan-op : RelOp,
    plan-avgs : List Text,
    plan-diags : List LensDiag
  }

  lp-fail : List LensDiag -> LensPlanResult
  lp-fail (ds) = LensPlanResult { plan-ok = False, plan-op = RelScan "", plan-avgs = [], plan-diags = ds }

  lp-good : RelOp, List Text -> LensPlanResult
  lp-good (op) (avgs) = LensPlanResult { plan-ok = True, plan-op = op, plan-avgs = avgs, plan-diags = [] }

Section: Name Resolution

 Query names resolve against the model's declared dimensions and
 measures. Every unknown name earns its own diagnostic so the analyst
 sees the whole damage in one pass.

  lp-dim-idx : List LensDimension, Integer, Text -> Integer
  lp-dim-idx (ds) (i) (nm) =
    if i >= list-length ds then -1
    else let d = list-at ds i
    in if d.name == nm then i
    else lp-dim-idx ds (i + 1) nm

  lp-measure-idx : List LensMeasure, Integer, Text -> Integer
  lp-measure-idx (ms) (i) (nm) =
    if i >= list-length ms then -1
    else let m = list-at ms i
    in if m.name == nm then i
    else lp-measure-idx ms (i + 1) nm

  LpDims = record {
    lpd-dims : List LensDimension,
    lpd-diags : List LensDiag
  }

  lp-resolve-dims : LensModel, List Text, Integer, List LensDimension, List LensDiag -> LpDims
  lp-resolve-dims (model) (names) (i) (acc) (diags) =
    if i >= list-length names then LpDims { lpd-dims = acc, lpd-diags = diags }
    else let nm = list-at names i
    in let idx = lp-dim-idx (model.dimensions) 0 nm
    in if idx < 0 then lp-resolve-dims model names (i + 1) acc (list-push diags (lens-diag 21 ("unknown dimension " & nm)))
    else lp-resolve-dims model names (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at (model.dimensions) idx)) diags

  LpMeasures = record {
    lpm-measures : List LensMeasure,
    lpm-diags : List LensDiag
  }

  lp-resolve-measures : LensModel, List Text, Integer, List LensMeasure, List LensDiag -> LpMeasures
  lp-resolve-measures (model) (names) (i) (acc) (diags) =
    if i >= list-length names then LpMeasures { lpm-measures = acc, lpm-diags = diags }
    else let nm = list-at names i
    in let idx = lp-measure-idx (model.measures) 0 nm
    in if idx < 0 then lp-resolve-measures model names (i + 1) acc (list-push diags (lens-diag 22 ("unknown measure " & nm)))
    else lp-resolve-measures model names (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at (model.measures) idx)) diags

Section: Join Paths

 The planner trusts chains of declared many-to-one joins walked out
 of a measure's home table. lp-find-paths enumerates the distinct
 chains from one table to another by a depth-first walk over the
 model's join list: each step follows a many-to-one join out of the
 current table, the visited list forbids returning to a table so no
 walk cycles, and the depth counter caps a chain at four hops. The
 walk stops collecting at two paths, because one path is a plan and
 two is diagnostic 28 no matter how many more exist; the accumulator
 never grows past two, so the search is bounded by the join list, the
 depth cap, and the path cap together. A path is the list of join
 indices walked, in order, and lp-render-path spells one out as the
 table names it passes through.

  lp-join-hop : LensJoin, Text -> Boolean
  lp-join-hop (j) (from) =
    if j.from-table == from then
      when j.cardinality
        is ManyToOne -> True
        is otherwise -> False
    else False

  lp-path-step : List LensJoin, Text, Text, Integer, List Text, List Integer, List (List Integer) -> List (List Integer)
  lp-path-step (js) (cur) (target) (depth) (visited) (path) (acc) =
    if list-length acc >= 2 then acc
    else if cur == target then list-push acc path
    else if depth <= 0 then acc
    else lp-path-scan js cur target depth visited path acc 0

  lp-path-scan : List LensJoin, Text, Text, Integer, List Text, List Integer, List (List Integer), Integer -> List (List Integer)
  lp-path-scan (js) (cur) (target) (depth) (visited) (path) (acc) (i) =
    if i >= list-length js then acc
    else let j = list-at js i
    in if lp-join-hop j cur == False then lp-path-scan js cur target depth visited path acc (i + 1)
    else if lp-texts-contain visited 0 (j.to-table) then lp-path-scan js cur target depth visited path acc (i + 1)
    else let sub = lp-path-step js (j.to-table) target (depth - 1) (list-push visited (j.to-table)) (list-push path i) acc
    in lp-path-scan js cur target depth visited path sub (i + 1)

  lp-find-paths : List LensJoin, Text, Text -> List (List Integer)
  lp-find-paths (js) (from) (to) = lp-path-step js from to 4 [from] [] []

  lp-render-path : List LensJoin, List Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  lp-render-path (js) (path) (k) (acc) =
    if k >= list-length path then acc
    else let j = list-at js (list-at path k)
    in lp-render-path js path (k + 1) (acc & " -> " & j.to-table)

Section: Grain Checking

 The grain checker refuses every query the builder below cannot plan
 correctly. It walks each measure against each requested dimension: a
 dimension on the measure's own table is always fine, a dimension
 whose table exactly one many-to-one chain reaches is fine, a table
 no chain reaches is code 23, and a table two chains reach is code
 28 with both offending paths named, so the analyst sees the
 ambiguity spelled out instead of a silently chosen join.

  lp-check-reach : LensModel, List LensDimension, LensMeasure, Integer, List LensDiag -> List LensDiag
  lp-check-reach (model) (dims) (m) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length dims then acc
    else let d = list-at dims i
    in if d.table == m.table then lp-check-reach model dims m (i + 1) acc
    else let paths = lp-find-paths (model.joins) (m.table) (d.table)
    in if list-length paths == 1 then lp-check-reach model dims m (i + 1) acc
    else if list-length paths == 0 then lp-check-reach model dims m (i + 1) (list-push acc (lens-diag 23 ("measure " & m.name & " on table " & m.table & " cannot reach dimension " & d.name & " on table " & d.table & ": no many-to-one join chain declared")))
    else lp-check-reach model dims m (i + 1) (list-push acc (lens-diag 28 ("measure " & m.name & " on table " & m.table & " reaches dimension " & d.name & " on table " & d.table & " by more than one many-to-one path: " & lp-render-path (model.joins) (list-at paths 0) 0 (m.table) & " and " & lp-render-path (model.joins) (list-at paths 1) 0 (m.table))))

  lp-check-measures : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensMeasure, Integer, List LensDiag -> List LensDiag
  lp-check-measures (model) (dims) (ms) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ms then acc
    else lp-check-measures model dims ms (i + 1) (lp-check-reach model dims (list-at ms i) 0 acc)

  lp-grain-check : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensMeasure -> List LensDiag
  lp-grain-check (model) (dims) (ms) =
    lp-check-measures model dims ms 0 []

Section: Aggregate Mapping

 The model's Lens-prefixed aggregation kinds map onto the relational
 algebra's aggregate functions twice: once at the home grain over the
 raw column, and once at re-aggregation time over the alias the first
 pass produced. Count re-aggregates as a sum of per-key counts. An
 average never reaches either map: lp-agg-specs decomposes it into a
 sum aliased with the __sum suffix and a count aliased with the __cnt
 suffix, and lp-reagg-specs re-aggregates both aliases as sums, which
 is lossless where re-aggregating an average is not. The AggAvg arms
 below are therefore unreachable and exist so the matches stay total.

  lp-is-avg : AggKind -> Boolean
  lp-is-avg (k) =
    when k
      is LensAggAvg -> True
      is otherwise -> False

  lp-avg-sum-col : Text -> Text
  lp-avg-sum-col (nm) = nm & "__sum"

  lp-avg-cnt-col : Text -> Text
  lp-avg-cnt-col (nm) = nm & "__cnt"

  lp-agg-func : AggKind, Text -> AggFunc
  lp-agg-func (k) (col) =
    when k
      is LensAggSum -> AggSum col
      is LensAggCount -> AggCount
      is LensAggAvg -> AggAvg col
      is LensAggMin -> AggMin col
      is LensAggMax -> AggMax col

  lp-reagg-func : AggKind, Text -> AggFunc
  lp-reagg-func (k) (col) =
    when k
      is LensAggSum -> AggSum col
      is LensAggCount -> AggSum col
      is LensAggAvg -> AggAvg col
      is LensAggMin -> AggMin col
      is LensAggMax -> AggMax col

  lp-agg-spec : LensMeasure -> AggSpec
  lp-agg-spec (m) = AggSpec { agg-func = lp-agg-func (m.agg) (m.column), agg-alias = m.name }

  lp-reagg-spec : LensMeasure -> AggSpec
  lp-reagg-spec (m) = AggSpec { agg-func = lp-reagg-func (m.agg) (m.name), agg-alias = m.name }

  lp-agg-specs : LensMeasure -> List AggSpec
  lp-agg-specs (m) =
    if lp-is-avg (m.agg) == False then [lp-agg-spec m]
    else [AggSpec { agg-func = AggSum (m.column), agg-alias = lp-avg-sum-col (m.name) }, AggSpec { agg-func = AggCount, agg-alias = lp-avg-cnt-col (m.name) }]

  lp-reagg-specs : LensMeasure -> List AggSpec
  lp-reagg-specs (m) =
    if lp-is-avg (m.agg) == False then [lp-reagg-spec m]
    else [AggSpec { agg-func = AggSum (lp-avg-sum-col (m.name)), agg-alias = lp-avg-sum-col (m.name) }, AggSpec { agg-func = AggSum (lp-avg-cnt-col (m.name)), agg-alias = lp-avg-cnt-col (m.name) }]

Section: Bucketed Dimensions

 A bucketed dimension reads its date column through a calendar
 bucket, and its effective column everywhere in the plan is an
 alias: the physical column name, two underscores, and the bucket
 word, so a month bucket over order-date answers to
 order-date__month. The alias is what group keys, display columns,
 combine-join columns, and sort columns carry, because the bucketed
 value is a new column the derive computes, not a reading of the old
 one. The derive itself sits directly on the filtered scan of the
 dimension's home table, under every aggregation, so bucket values
 exist at raw-row grain before any group or join touches them: a
 home-table bucket is derived under the measure's home-grain group,
 and a foreign bucket is derived on the dimension table's own scan
 before the equi-join reaches it. Filters keep naming physical
 columns and sit under the derive, which is harmless because the
 derive only appends columns. Declaring a bucket is the modeler's
 assertion the column holds Unix seconds, per the model chapter; no
 planner diagnostic polices it. The LbNone arm of lp-bucket-fn is
 unreachable because every caller checks lp-dim-bucketed first; the
 arm answers DerYear so the match stays total.

  lp-dim-bucketed : LensDimension -> Boolean
  lp-dim-bucketed (d) =
    when d.bucket
      is LbNone -> False
      is otherwise -> True

  lp-bucket-suffix : LensBucket -> Text
  lp-bucket-suffix (b) =
    when b
      is LbNone -> ""
      is LbYear -> "year"
      is LbQuarter -> "quarter"
      is LbMonth -> "month"
      is LbDay -> "day"

  lp-bucket-fn : LensBucket -> DeriveFn
  lp-bucket-fn (b) =
    when b
      is LbNone -> DerYear
      is LbYear -> DerYear
      is LbQuarter -> DerQuarter
      is LbMonth -> DerMonth
      is LbDay -> DerDay

  lp-dim-col : LensDimension -> Text
  lp-dim-col (d) =
    if lp-dim-bucketed d then d.column & "__" & lp-bucket-suffix (d.bucket)
    else d.column

  lp-derive-specs : List LensDimension, Text, Integer, List DeriveSpec -> List DeriveSpec
  lp-derive-specs (dims) (tbl) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length dims then acc
    else let d = list-at dims i
    in if d.table == tbl then
      (if lp-dim-bucketed d then lp-derive-specs dims tbl (i + 1) (list-push acc (DeriveSpec { der-alias = lp-dim-col d, der-col = d.column, der-fn = lp-bucket-fn (d.bucket) })) else lp-derive-specs dims tbl (i + 1) acc)
    else lp-derive-specs dims tbl (i + 1) acc

  lp-derived-scan : List LensDimension, List LensFilter, Text -> RelOp
  lp-derived-scan (dims) (fs) (tbl) =
    let specs = lp-derive-specs dims tbl 0 []
    in if list-length specs == 0 then lp-filtered-scan fs tbl
    else RelDerive (lp-filtered-scan fs tbl) specs

Section: Column Bookkeeping

 Small text-list helpers: membership and push-if-absent, so group
 keys and attached tables stay duplicate-free. The home-side group
 key for a foreign dimension is the first hop's left column, because
 only that column lives on the home table; the later hops' keys ride
 along on the joined dimension tables. The builder runs only after
 the grain check proved exactly one path exists, so taking the first
 found path is taking the only one. lp-measure-cols lists the columns
 the plan itself produces per measure: the measure name, except an
 average contributes its sum and count aliases because the division
 happens after execution.

  lp-texts-contain : List Text, Integer, Text -> Boolean
  lp-texts-contain (ts) (i) (nm) =
    if i >= list-length ts then False
    else if list-at ts i == nm then True
    else lp-texts-contain ts (i + 1) nm

  lp-push-unique : List Text, Text -> List Text
  lp-push-unique (ts) (nm) =
    if lp-texts-contain ts 0 nm then ts else list-push ts nm

  lp-home-col : LensModel, Text, LensDimension -> Text
  lp-home-col (model) (home) (d) =
    if d.table == home then lp-dim-col d
    else let path = list-at (lp-find-paths (model.joins) home (d.table)) 0
    in let j = list-at (model.joins) (list-at path 0)
    in j.on-left

  lp-group-keys : LensModel, List LensDimension, Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  lp-group-keys (model) (dims) (home) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length dims then acc
    else let d = list-at dims i
    in lp-group-keys model dims home (i + 1) (lp-push-unique acc (lp-home-col model home d))

  lp-display-cols : List LensDimension, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  lp-display-cols (dims) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length dims then acc
    else let d = list-at dims i
    in lp-display-cols dims (i + 1) (lp-push-unique acc (lp-dim-col d))

  lp-measure-cols : List LensMeasure, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  lp-measure-cols (ms) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ms then acc
    else let m = list-at ms i
    in if lp-is-avg (m.agg) then lp-measure-cols ms (i + 1) (list-push (list-push acc (lp-avg-sum-col (m.name))) (lp-avg-cnt-col (m.name)))
    else lp-measure-cols ms (i + 1) (list-push acc (m.name))

Section: Filters

 Filter checking walks every filter three ways. The filter's table
 must be declared. The filter's column must be part of the model's
 vocabulary for that table: the table's primary key, a declared
 dimension or measure column on the table, or a declared join key
 touching the table. The table must take part in the query, as some
 measure's home table or some requested dimension's table, because a
 filter on an absent table would otherwise be dropped silently and
 the numbers would answer a different question than the one asked.
 Each failing filter earns diagnostic 27.

  lp-filter-col-known : LensModel, Text, Text -> Boolean
  lp-filter-col-known (model) (tbl) (col) =
    if table-pk (model.tables) tbl == col then True
    else if lp-dim-col-within (model.dimensions) 0 tbl col then True
    else if lp-measure-col-within (model.measures) 0 tbl col then True
    else lp-join-col-within (model.joins) 0 tbl col

  lp-dim-col-within : List LensDimension, Integer, Text, Text -> Boolean
  lp-dim-col-within (ds) (i) (tbl) (col) =
    if i >= list-length ds then False
    else let d = list-at ds i
    in if d.table == tbl then (if d.column == col then True else lp-dim-col-within ds (i + 1) tbl col)
    else lp-dim-col-within ds (i + 1) tbl col

  lp-measure-col-within : List LensMeasure, Integer, Text, Text -> Boolean
  lp-measure-col-within (ms) (i) (tbl) (col) =
    if i >= list-length ms then False
    else let m = list-at ms i
    in if m.table == tbl then (if m.column == col then True else lp-measure-col-within ms (i + 1) tbl col)
    else lp-measure-col-within ms (i + 1) tbl col

  lp-join-col-within : List LensJoin, Integer, Text, Text -> Boolean
  lp-join-col-within (js) (i) (tbl) (col) =
    if i >= list-length js then False
    else let j = list-at js i
    in if j.from-table == tbl then (if j.on-left == col then True else lp-join-col-within js (i + 1) tbl col)
    else if j.to-table == tbl then (if j.on-right == col then True else lp-join-col-within js (i + 1) tbl col)
    else lp-join-col-within js (i + 1) tbl col

  lp-filter-table-used : List LensDimension, List LensMeasure, Text -> Boolean
  lp-filter-table-used (dims) (ms) (tbl) =
    if lp-dim-table-within dims 0 tbl then True
    else lp-measure-home-within ms 0 tbl

  lp-dim-table-within : List LensDimension, Integer, Text -> Boolean
  lp-dim-table-within (ds) (i) (tbl) =
    if i >= list-length ds then False
    else let d = list-at ds i
    in if d.table == tbl then True
    else lp-dim-table-within ds (i + 1) tbl

  lp-measure-home-within : List LensMeasure, Integer, Text -> Boolean
  lp-measure-home-within (ms) (i) (tbl) =
    if i >= list-length ms then False
    else let m = list-at ms i
    in if m.table == tbl then True
    else lp-measure-home-within ms (i + 1) tbl

  lp-check-filters : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensMeasure, List LensFilter, Integer, List LensDiag -> List LensDiag
  lp-check-filters (model) (dims) (ms) (fs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length fs then acc
    else let f = list-at fs i
    in let a1 = if table-declared (model.tables) (f.table) == False
         then list-push acc (lens-diag 27 ("filter names undeclared table " & f.table))
         else if lp-filter-col-known model (f.table) (f.column) == False
         then list-push acc (lens-diag 27 ("filter column " & f.column & " is not in the model vocabulary for table " & f.table))
         else if lp-filter-table-used dims ms (f.table) == False
         then list-push acc (lens-diag 27 ("filter table " & f.table & " takes no part in this query"))
         else acc
    in lp-check-filters model dims ms fs (i + 1) a1

 A checked filter becomes a column-versus-literal equality predicate,
 and lp-filtered-scan wraps a table scan in one RelFilter per filter
 naming that table. Every scan the builder emits goes through
 lp-filtered-scan, therefore filters sit under the aggregations by
 construction.

  lp-filter-pred : LensFilter -> Predicate
  lp-filter-pred (f) =
    when f.value
      is LfInt (n) -> PredColCmp (f.column) CmpEq (ValInteger n)
      is LfText (t) -> PredColCmp (f.column) CmpEq (ValText t)

  lp-filtered-scan : List LensFilter, Text -> RelOp
  lp-filtered-scan (fs) (tbl) = lp-filtered-scan-loop fs tbl 0 (RelScan tbl)

  lp-filtered-scan-loop : List LensFilter, Text, Integer, RelOp -> RelOp
  lp-filtered-scan-loop (fs) (tbl) (i) (op) =
    if i >= list-length fs then op
    else let f = list-at fs i
    in if f.table == tbl then lp-filtered-scan-loop fs tbl (i + 1) (RelFilter op (lp-filter-pred f))
    else lp-filtered-scan-loop fs tbl (i + 1) op

Section: Per-Measure Plans

 One measure becomes one aggregated sub-plan keyed by the requested
 dimension columns. The no-join case is a single group over the home
 table. The join case is the three-step ladder the chapter opened
 with: group the home table by the join keys and any home dimension
 columns, equi-join along each dimension's join chain one hop at a
 time, then group again by the dimension display columns with the
 re-aggregation functions over the aliases the first group produced.
 A table an earlier chain already joined is never joined twice: the
 done list carries every attached table across chains, so two
 dimensions whose chains share a prefix share the joined tables too,
 and the shared table's columns carry the later hops' join keys.
 Every scan in either case is a filtered scan, therefore query
 filters restrict rows before any grouping runs, and every scan of a
 table hosting a requested bucketed dimension is additionally a
 derived scan, therefore bucket columns exist before any grouping or
 joining reads them.

  lp-needs-join : List LensDimension, Text, Integer -> Boolean
  lp-needs-join (dims) (home) (i) =
    if i >= list-length dims then False
    else let d = list-at dims i
    in if d.table /= home then True
    else lp-needs-join dims home (i + 1)

  LpAttach = record {
    lap-op : RelOp,
    lap-done : List Text
  }

  lp-attach-path : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensFilter, RelOp, List Integer, Integer, List Text -> LpAttach
  lp-attach-path (model) (dims) (fs) (op) (path) (k) (done) =
    if k >= list-length path then LpAttach { lap-op = op, lap-done = done }
    else let j = list-at (model.joins) (list-at path k)
    in if lp-texts-contain done 0 (j.to-table) then lp-attach-path model dims fs op path (k + 1) done
    else lp-attach-path model dims fs (RelEquiJoin op (lp-derived-scan dims fs (j.to-table)) [j.on-left] [j.on-right]) path (k + 1) (list-push done (j.to-table))

  lp-attach-dims : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensFilter, Text, RelOp, Integer, List Text -> RelOp
  lp-attach-dims (model) (dims) (fs) (home) (op) (i) (done) =
    if i >= list-length dims then op
    else let d = list-at dims i
    in if d.table == home then lp-attach-dims model dims fs home op (i + 1) done
    else if lp-texts-contain done 0 (d.table) then lp-attach-dims model dims fs home op (i + 1) done
    else let path = list-at (lp-find-paths (model.joins) home (d.table)) 0
    in let att = lp-attach-path model dims fs op path 0 done
    in lp-attach-dims model dims fs home (att.lap-op) (i + 1) (att.lap-done)

  lp-measure-plan : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensFilter, LensMeasure -> RelOp
  lp-measure-plan (model) (dims) (fs) (m) =
    if lp-needs-join dims (m.table) 0 == False
    then RelGroup (lp-derived-scan dims fs (m.table)) (lp-display-cols dims 0 []) (lp-agg-specs m)
    else let keys = lp-group-keys model dims (m.table) 0 []
    in let grained = RelGroup (lp-derived-scan dims fs (m.table)) keys (lp-agg-specs m)
    in let joined = lp-attach-dims model dims fs (m.table) grained 0 []
    in RelGroup joined (lp-display-cols dims 0 []) (lp-reagg-specs m)

Section: Assembly

 Measure sub-plans combine pairwise. With dimensions present the
 combine is an equi-join on the full list of dimension display
 columns, therefore several measures with several dimensions pair up
 exactly; with no dimensions each sub-plan is a single row and a
 cross join through an always-true predicate glues them side by side.
 After combining: project the dimension columns and the per-measure
 plan columns, sort ascending by the dimensions, and apply a positive
 limit. An average's sum and count columns both survive the
 projection; lens-run collapses them after execution.

  lp-measure-plans : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensFilter, List LensMeasure, Integer, List RelOp -> List RelOp
  lp-measure-plans (model) (dims) (fs) (ms) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ms then acc
    else lp-measure-plans model dims fs ms (i + 1) (list-push acc (lp-measure-plan model dims fs (list-at ms i)))

  lp-combine : List RelOp, List Text, Integer, RelOp -> RelOp
  lp-combine (plans) (dcols) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length plans then acc
    else let p = list-at plans i
    in if list-length dcols == 0 then lp-combine plans dcols (i + 1) (RelJoin acc p PredTrue)
    else lp-combine plans dcols (i + 1) (RelEquiJoin acc p dcols dcols)

  lp-sort-specs : List Text, Integer, List SortSpec -> List SortSpec
  lp-sort-specs (cols) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length cols then acc
    else lp-sort-specs cols (i + 1) (list-push acc (SortSpec { sort-col = list-at cols i, sort-dir = SortAsc }))

  lp-assemble : LensModel, List LensDimension, List LensFilter, List LensMeasure, Integer -> RelOp
  lp-assemble (model) (dims) (fs) (ms) (limit) =
    let plans = lp-measure-plans model dims fs ms 0 []
    in let dcols = lp-display-cols dims 0 []
    in let combined = lp-combine plans dcols 1 (list-at plans 0)
    in let projected = RelProject combined (proj-columns (dcols & lp-measure-cols ms 0 []))
    in let sorted = if list-length dcols == 0 then projected else RelSort projected (lp-sort-specs dcols 0 [])
    in if limit > 0 then RelLimit sorted limit else sorted

Section: The Planner

 lens-plan is the whole contract: validate the model, resolve the
 query's names, grain-check alongside filter-check, and only then
 build. The first failing stage answers alone, so a diagnostic list
 never mixes model faults with query faults. A good plan carries the
 names of its average measures so lens-run knows which column pairs
 to divide.

  lp-avg-names : List LensMeasure, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  lp-avg-names (ms) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ms then acc
    else let m = list-at ms i
    in lp-avg-names ms (i + 1) (if lp-is-avg (m.agg) then list-push acc (m.name) else acc)

  lens-plan : LensModel, LensQuery -> LensPlanResult
  lens-plan (model) (q) =
    let vd = lens-validate model
    in if list-length vd > 0 then lp-fail vd
    else if q.lens-name /= model.name then lp-fail [lens-diag 20 ("unknown lens " & q.lens-name & ": this model declares " & model.name)]
    else let rd = lp-resolve-dims model (q.dimensions) 0 [] []
    in let rm = lp-resolve-measures model (q.measures) 0 [] []
    in let named = (rd.lpd-diags) & (rm.lpm-diags)
    in let counted = if list-length (q.measures) == 0 then list-push named (lens-diag 24 "query names no measures") else named
    in if list-length counted > 0 then lp-fail counted
    else let grained = lp-check-filters model (rd.lpd-dims) (rm.lpm-measures) (q.filters) 0 (lp-grain-check model (rd.lpd-dims) (rm.lpm-measures))
    in if list-length grained > 0 then lp-fail grained
    else lp-good (lp-assemble model (rd.lpd-dims) (q.filters) (rm.lpm-measures) (q.limit)) (lp-avg-names (rm.lpm-measures) 0 [])

Section: Execution

 lens-run drives a query end to end against a live catalog. A failed
 plan surfaces as a query error carrying every diagnostic, code and
 message both, so no caller ever executes a placeholder plan. A plan
 carrying average measures comes back from the engine with each
 average still split into its sum and count columns; lp-finish-avgs
 rewrites the result once, after every join, combine, sort, and limit
 has already happened: the sum column becomes the measure-name column
 holding sum divided by count, the count column disappears, and every
 other column passes through untouched. The division is integer
 division in v1, the same truncation the engine's own average
 applies. A count of zero would mean a group no row ever landed in,
 which grouping never produces; the guard answers ValNull rather
 than divide by zero.

  lp-render-diags : List LensDiag, Integer, Text -> Text
  lp-render-diags (ds) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ds then acc
    else let d = list-at ds i
    in let line = "diag " & show (d.code) & ": " & d.message
    in lp-render-diags ds (i + 1) (if i == 0 then line else acc & "; " & line)

  lp-avg-sum-base : List Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  lp-avg-sum-base (avgs) (i) (col) =
    if i >= list-length avgs then ""
    else let a = list-at avgs i
    in if col == lp-avg-sum-col a then a
    else lp-avg-sum-base avgs (i + 1) col

  lp-avg-cnt-hit : List Text, Integer, Text -> Boolean
  lp-avg-cnt-hit (avgs) (i) (col) =
    if i >= list-length avgs then False
    else if col == lp-avg-cnt-col (list-at avgs i) then True
    else lp-avg-cnt-hit avgs (i + 1) col

  lp-avg-fix-cols : List Text, List ColumnType, List Text, Integer, List Text, List ColumnType -> RowSchema
  lp-avg-fix-cols (names) (types) (avgs) (i) (out-names) (out-types) =
    if i >= list-length names then schema-new out-names out-types
    else let nm = list-at names i
    in let base = lp-avg-sum-base avgs 0 nm
    in if base /= "" then lp-avg-fix-cols names types avgs (i + 1) (list-push out-names base) (list-push out-types ColInteger)
    else if lp-avg-cnt-hit avgs 0 nm then lp-avg-fix-cols names types avgs (i + 1) out-names out-types
    else lp-avg-fix-cols names types avgs (i + 1) (list-push out-names nm) (list-push out-types (list-at types i))

  lp-avg-fix-schema : RowSchema, List Text -> RowSchema
  lp-avg-fix-schema (s) (avgs) = lp-avg-fix-cols (s.col-names) (s.col-types) avgs 0 [] []

  lp-avg-divide : RowData, Text -> ColumnValue
  lp-avg-divide (row) (base) =
    let s = val-to-integer (row-get-by-name row (lp-avg-sum-col base))
    in let c = val-to-integer (row-get-by-name row (lp-avg-cnt-col base))
    in if c == 0 then ValNull else ValInteger (s / c)

  lp-avg-fix-vals : RowData, List Text, Integer, List ColumnValue -> List ColumnValue
  lp-avg-fix-vals (row) (avgs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length (row.values) then acc
    else let nm = list-at (row.schema.col-names) i
    in let base = lp-avg-sum-base avgs 0 nm
    in if base /= "" then lp-avg-fix-vals row avgs (i + 1) (list-push acc (lp-avg-divide row base))
    else if lp-avg-cnt-hit avgs 0 nm then lp-avg-fix-vals row avgs (i + 1) acc
    else lp-avg-fix-vals row avgs (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at (row.values) i))

  lp-avg-fix-rows : List RowData, RowSchema, List Text, Integer, List RowData -> List RowData
  lp-avg-fix-rows (rows) (fixed) (avgs) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length rows then acc
    else let row = list-at rows i
    in lp-avg-fix-rows rows fixed avgs (i + 1) (list-push acc (row-new fixed (lp-avg-fix-vals row avgs 0 [])))

  lp-finish-avgs : QueryResult, List Text -> QueryResult
  lp-finish-avgs (qr) (avgs) =
    if list-length avgs == 0 then qr
    else if qr.qr-ok == False then qr
    else let fixed = lp-avg-fix-schema (qr.qr-schema) avgs
    in qr-ok (lp-avg-fix-rows (qr.qr-rows) fixed avgs 0 []) fixed

  lens-run : Catalog, LensModel, LensQuery -> QueryResult
  lens-run (cat) (model) (q) =
    let pr = lens-plan model q
    in if pr.plan-ok == False then qr-error ("lens-plan: " & lp-render-diags (pr.plan-diags) 0 "")
    else lp-finish-avgs (query cat (pr.plan-op)) (pr.plan-avgs)

